osts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:31:21-07:00","id":966347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966338#post966338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My guess it 2 to lock it to yourself, 3 to lock it to someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely.<br /> It follows the more or less usual 2/3/4 division.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:46:59-07:00","id":966354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966328#post966328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if I do extended rolls to stack up successes. my diff rises by +1 even if it's not turn per turn roll? also paradox stacks up with each extended rolls I do or it only backslashes as 2 paradox pt (yes no witnesses) even if I did 3-4 extended rolls? (asking in general in case vulgar magick yes). Thanks in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And this please?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:50:38-07:00","id":966357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966329#post966329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't the shield still bump into things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. It still would! Which might be mighty awkward unless it's designed to only stop forces of a certain magnitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:58:36-07:00","id":966360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966328#post966328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if I do extended rolls to stack up successes. my diff rises by +1 even if it's not turn per turn roll? also paradox stacks up with each extended rolls I do or it only backslashes as 2 paradox pt (yes no witnesses) even if I did 3-4 extended rolls? (asking in general in case vulgar magick yes). Thanks in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you use a brief rite or a ceremony (types of rituals) you do not get the diff increase. The stacking paradox is for a botch, if you do not botch and no interference happens(interference counts as botch if you do ritual magick) then you get the usual 2 dox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:50:05-07:00","id":966395,"title":"","content":"Appreciated. What about extended rolls with magickal spells like fireballs, lightning bolts... etc. You still get +1 diff when it's turn per turn, right? and if it's not turn per turn you don't get +1 and it's considered a ritual or what cuz this part is so confusing tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:55:37-07:00","id":966399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966395#post966395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appreciated. What about extended rolls with magickal spells like fireballs, lightning bolts... etc. You still get +1 diff when it's turn per turn, right? and if it's not turn per turn you don't get +1 and it's considered a ritual or what cuz this part is so confusing tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I forgo the whole &quot;+1 diff per extended Arete roll&quot; thing until they reach higher than 10 successes because otherwise anyone with bellow Arete 5 can't really do a damn thing.<br /> <br /> The biggest difference between a ritual and just extended Arete rolls is that extended Arete rolls is being done &quot;on the fly&quot; so to speak. It's the &quot;need big effect now!&quot; approach to magic, while rituals have to be planned out and require much more time to employ.<br /> <br /> This extra time between rolls ensures that it's easier to do them, i.e. difficulty stays fairly consistent. It also allows several mages to contribute to a single effect.<br /> <br /> Another difference is that certain effects may become coincidental as a result. One guy forcing a ghost to appear? That's creepy and weird. But a whole host of people doing it over the course of an hour? That's a seance, perfectly normal (kinda).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:02:40-07:00","id":966427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966399#post966399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Personally, I forgo the whole &quot;+1 diff per extended Arete roll&quot; thing until they reach higher than 10 successes because otherwise anyone with bellow Arete 5 can't really do a damn thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? Rituals don't get the +1 diff per roll. Only non-ritual by-'turn' extended Arete rolls do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And going by M20, that gives you quite enough wallop, especially if you have Quintessence to spare.<br /> You are quite right though if you use the Revised-system split-succeses rule, as that one demands a lot of succeses for even small things, sadly. Revised was ritual-tastic because of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:13:22-07:00","id":966429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966427#post966427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh? Rituals don't get the +1 diff per roll. Only non-ritual by-'turn' extended Arete rolls do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And going by M20, that gives you quite enough wallop, especially if you have Quintessence to spare.<br /> You are quite right though if you use the Revised-system split-succeses rule, as that one demands a lot of succeses for even small things, sadly. Revised was ritual-tastic because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Revised is the system I go by for most things. It's the first system I played and the one I'm most familiar with.<br /> I know Rituals don't get the +1 diff, I said as much in my post (that's the bit that says difficulty stays fairly consistent, though I get why that can be misconstrued.<br /> <br /> How does M20 divvy up successes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:31:51-07:00","id":966437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966429#post966429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does M20 divvy up successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 is like the older Second Edition, or Sorceror's Crusade - You still need to divide successes between Damage and Duration if you want *both* of them to apply at once - but aside of that the default rule is that the *total* successes count for everything. It really simplifies things, and makes Mages with low Arete scores not need tons of rolls to pull off everyday things. Of course there are still certain minimum amounts of successes to be reached, depending on the magnitude of the feat.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Revised &quot;Divided Successes&quot; system is an optional rule that you can either still optionally use, enforce, or the ST can decide to mix and match - for example, they can still demand one extra success per extra target on top of the rest of the successes, but leave the rest as is. But the default rule is as above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-09-2016, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:36:07-07:00","id":966464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966305#post966305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, its a Forces 2 effect. How exactly this would work is never stated in raw, but you could make it as soak dices, or reducing damage from the opponent. There are lots of ways, actually.<br /> <br /> Also, the shield would probably push everytjing that goes around the mage, depending on how it ws made, which could be quite annoying</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC in revised it negates damage at an equal rate to dealing damage. So firebolt does 3 damage, fire shield deflects 3 damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:50:41-07:00","id":966523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966464#post966464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC in revised it negates damage at an equal rate to dealing damage. So firebolt does 3 damage, fire shield deflects 3 damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can I find this rule, I don't remember this. So, with 2 successes you can create a shield that deflects 4 damage and then it's gone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:05:03-07:00","id":967694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966305#post966305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, its a Forces 2 effect. How exactly this would work is never stated in raw, but you could make it as soak dices, or reducing damage from the opponent. There are lots of ways, actually.<br /> <br /> Also, the shield would probably push everytjing that goes around the mage, depending on how it ws made, which could be quite annoying</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always ruled it depends on paradigm and personality of the mage in question.<br /> <br /> A Tytalan NPC in a previous Mage game had a straight-up <i>Parma Magicka</i> style ablative barrier with auto-soak levels, but had to be restored via Arete rolls as it ablated. In other words, she had magickal reactive armor. But, her preference was to hit hard and hit fast, and be able to soak up individual <i>huge</i> hits that may or may not happen before she had the chance to lay her opponent out...or her personal favorite trick, tie in Mind Effects to compel her enemies to surrender, having seen her negate those massive hits. Vulgar, but effective.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, her Flambeau NPC best friend preferred shields (Forces 2/Prime 3) which siphoned away the Forces Pattern of incoming attacks as ambient Quintessence, which she could then throw back at her targets. It didn't negate the attack, thereby keeping it coincidental (important for a Flambeau who needed the ability to skimp on Paradox she could instead build up through attacking), but it <i>did</i> jack up the difficulty of damage rolls made against her and allowed her to use &quot;ambient Quintessence&quot; to fuel magic without fucking up the surrounding environment (at least, due to loss of Quintessence).<br /> <br /> In the same chronicle, a Euthanatos PC used a combined Entropy/Forces Effect to subtly bleed off the kinetic energy of attacks while increasing the probability the attacker would miss. Sure, either sphere independently could work...but Forces, unless one spends valuable successes, can only target one type of Forces Pattern at a time, and Entropy only goes so far against area-affecting attacks. Not to mention, depending on <i>what</i> is being employed against the mage, either sphere independently could invoke vulgarity; both at the same time, not necessarily so much. In any case, it was a flat difficulty hike to attack him.<br /> <br /> The VA PC used a Forces/Correspondence/Time Effect a time or two to imperceptibly dilate the space around him, causing the attack to move &quot;further&quot;, giving him a dodge difficulty reduction (the Forces component was to allow the Effect to be selective against what triggered it).<br /> <br /> Although, the nastiest and most inventive one employed in that chronicle was a Forces 2/Life 3 Effect which bled kinetic energy away from the attack to strengthen the mage's Life Pattern where the attack would hit. It provided soak difficulty reduction relative to the strength of the incoming hit, -1 for every two levels of damage dealt (to the usual minimum of 3). Which meant it was pretty much always coincidental, especially since it didn't negatively impact the mage's ability to interact with their surrounding world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T10:56:29-07:00","id":968017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=966330#post966330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its life 2 to lock the effect? not 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that for simple self-enhancements like this, conjunctional Life wouldn't be necessary. Similar to how you don't need conjunctional Life to teleport yourself with Correspondence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:01:01-07:00","id":968019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=968017#post968017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that for simple self-enhancements like this, conjunctional Life wouldn't be necessary. Similar to how you don't need conjunctional Life to teleport yourself with Correspondence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think this goes under the heading of &quot;Choose a rule and stick with it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:06:56-07:00","id":995799,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to make the barrier protect from physical AND a certain elemental such as fire too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:18:10-07:00","id":995854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=995799#post995799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to make the barrier protect from physical AND a certain elemental such as fire too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? It's all Forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T19:51:14-07:00","id":995923,"title":"","content":"At least in Revised, I recall them saying you could only block one type of force per casting. So you'd need a spell for kinetic energy, another for fire, another for electricity, still another to deflect light so you stay invisible, etc.<br /> <br /> Naturally, given that every Effects running simultaneously adds +1 to casting difficulties for all subsequent Arete rolls, and it's unlikely for any Mage to have protection from everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T01:54:50-07:00","id":996000,"title":"","content":"I would let it go, but you must score successes separately for each force with an upper limit of different forces equal to your Arete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T05:58:47-07:00","id":996042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=995923#post995923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least in Revised, I recall them saying you could only block one type of force per casting. So you'd need a spell for kinetic energy, another for fire, another for electricity, still another to deflect light so you stay invisible, etc.<br /> <br /> Naturally, given that every Effects running simultaneously adds +1 to casting difficulties for all subsequent Arete rolls, and it's unlikely for any Mage to have protection from everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually +1 for every two concurrent effects running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T06:50:53-07:00","id":996051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966293-kinetic-barrier-forces-2?p=996042#post996042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's actually +1 for every two concurrent effects running.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that exactly what I said?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:07:28-07:00","id":996074,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> You wrote &quot;Every Effects running&quot;, you must have neglected the &quot;2&quot; and I didn't notice the plural. oops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:25:24-07:00","id":996114,"title":"","content":"True. My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T06:36:54-07:00","id":996554,"title":"","content":"So, when you roll attribute+Ability to have reduction modifiers on your arete roll, it can negate that +1 or your max is still -3? like say you have diff 6 spell, you rolled attribute+ability and got 5 successes, did an extended roll, had -3 on the spell on your first turn roll then got +1 on the second roll, you can use one of your attribute+ability successes to negate that +1 and still roll at diff 3, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:44:14-07:00","id":996653,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12133\" data-vbnamecard=\"12133\">Leonardo</a> Exactly. But I experienced it to be handled differently at different tables.<br /> Your difficulty can not deviate more than 3 in either way from your base difficulty. Technically you can have a malus if 9 and a bonus of 12, resulting in a net modifier of 3 to your advantage.<br /> This is the reason why it is advantageous to get more than 3 successes for your slipstream effect. That way the attacks still go against 9 even if the attacker accrues a bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}